    "provinceDeepAtlasProfile": {
      "oneLine": "Zal’tharuun is centered at -60.995070, -104.773998 under Tribal Confederation, with 81,309,000 people across 14 settlements.",
      "extremeAtlasDescription": "Zal’tharuun occupies 10,763,398.02 sq mi / 27,877,072.91 sq km of modeled Earth-sized territory, about 5.465387% of Belavadös's surface. It is not merely a province but a continent-scale civic machine: Beach and grass with water, Ocean Surface floating settlement and Farming define its broad terrain, while its settlements intensify into Ocean Surface floating settlement, Beach and grass with water, Hybrid tree and forest floor, Underwater without reefs, Partial forest, and 1 more. Population density is 2.917 people/sq km / 7.554 people/sq mi, which lets wilderness, roads, faction-held corridors, and vast uncrowded borders remain huge.",
      "peopleFactionsAndFaith": "The strongest public people-groups are Humans, Near-Humans, and Mixed Heritage, Halfling and Smallfolk, Animalfolk and Mammalian Anthropomorphs, Amphibious and Aquatic Peoples, Elf Parent Race and Elf Bloodlines, Elemental and Energy-Born Peoples, and 2 more. Frequently recorded peoples include Human, Halfling — Lightfoot Halfling, Triton, Elf — Sea Elf, Tortle, Genasi — Water Genasi, Hadozee, Merfolk, and 4 more. Faction visibility leans toward The Obsidian Diadem, with worship and patronage records naming Nebyrr, Enkirael, Freyseth, Ishtanora, Iskareth, Bastveig, Sigrananna, and 3 more.",
      "groupLinkDescription": "The province participates in 5 recorded four-province geography group links, including 4 cross-transportation-group links. These links place it inside overlapping regional corridors rather than one isolated block, allowing border-adjacent transit, faction influence, and cultural spillover to breathe across group lines.",
